        "answer": "The student is incorrect. The passage is problem-solution, not cause-effect. Problem-solution names a difficulty (contaminated rivers) and presents remedies (the three cleanup strategies). Cause-effect would focus on explaining why the contamination occurred. The presence of proposed remedies is the decisive signal.",
