        "answer": "Compound: 'I like recess, and my friend likes recess, so we play every day.' Two or more independent clauses joined by coordinating conjunctions (and, so) is the defining feature of a compound sentence. Complex: 'Because we both like recess, my friend and I play every day.' A dependent clause introduced by a subordinating conjunction (because) attached to an independent clause is the hallmark of a complex sentence.",
